# Line endings.
#
# Git on Windows converts LF to CRLF in the working tree. That is harmless for
# Python, and fatal for a shell script that is about to become a container
# entrypoint: Linux reads the trailing \r as part of the interpreter path and
# the container dies with
#
#     exec /usr/local/bin/app-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# which points at a file that plainly exists. These files are LF, everywhere,
# regardless of who checks them out.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf

# Binary assets Git should never try to normalise.
*.png binary
*.db  binary
